  "summary": "OmniAuth: Host Header Injection Vulnerability",
  "details": "### Impact\nHost header injection risk when using Omniauth with a web framework that does not verify incoming host headers. An example of a framework that provides host header validation is modern Rails when [configured appropriately](https://guides.rubyonrails.org/v6.1.1/configuring.html#configuring-middleware)\n\n### Patches\n2.2.0\n\n### Workarounds\n_Set the `full_host` config in the Omniauth config_",
